{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — WHY THE HOMEPAGE BRAND BLOCK IS RENDERED FROM lbass-cro-tracking
  (documentation only — this snippet is never rendered)

  ══ THE PROBLEM ══
  templates/index.liquid declares {% layout none %} and emits its own complete
  HTML document — its own <html>, <head>, <title>, robots meta and footer.
  Measured 2026-08-05: 548KB rendered, of which the <head> alone is 249KB.

  Consequences, all verified on the live homepage:
    • layout/theme.liquid does not run on "/" at all
    • so the four-language entity block (lbass-entity-block) is on EVERY page
      EXCEPT the highest-authority one
    • so any <title> / meta description logic added to theme.liquid is inert
      for the homepage — index.liquid already emitted its own
    • shop.description is empty, so the homepage description is not coming
      from Admin either; it is hardcoded in index.liquid

  ══ WHY NOT JUST EDIT index.liquid ══
  The Admin API has no partial write — changing one line means uploading all
  226KB back. That is slow, and a single transcription slip silently corrupts
  a working storefront. Not worth it to insert one render call.

  ══ WHY lbass-cro-tracking IS THE RIGHT HOST ══
  It is one of the very few snippets rendered at BODY level by BOTH
  index.liquid and theme.liquid — its own header comment says so, and it is
  measurably the LAST thing in the homepage body (its </style> closes the
  document). That makes it the only cheap, server-rendered hook into the
  homepage.

  Server-rendered matters: the block has to be crawlable. Injecting it with
  JavaScript would work for Googlebot but is fragile, and content that only
  exists after JS runs is exactly the pattern this project has been avoiding.

  ══ STATUS (checked 2026-09-30) ══
  Superseded: templates/index.liquid now renders lbass-entity-block itself, in
  its own footer. And layout/theme.liquid does NOT render it, whatever earlier
  notes said: in this repo the entity block is on the homepage only. Putting
  it in the theme.liquid footer too is an open decision for the owner.

  The homepage <title> item once listed here is done: it now reads
  "Lbass Original | Friperie en ligne Maroc | Second-Hand من مراكش".
{%- endcomment -%}
